# Results of validate.py that are not "identical", for every build we have a
# static patch for. Builds that aren't listed must be identical.
#
# K3SysUi, Kobra 3 family: equivalent. The static patch also rewrites the
# unreachable tail of the old label, and on older builds returns through the
# Support row's closing branch instead of straight to where it goes.
#
# K3SysUi, Kobra 2 Pro: equivalent, for the second reason: the payload returns
# straight to the end of the row's code.
#
# K3SysUi, KS1 2.5.9.9, 2.6.0.0 and KS1M 2.1.6: DIFFERENT. The static patch
# hooks five instructions into the Support row, behind a row check that is
# always true there, and returns to the row's closing branch. Read side by
# side, both skip the page switch and continue at the row's exit.
#
# gkapi: declined where the build has no orcaSim server, so nothing listens on
# port 80. Those builds have no static gkapi patch either.
